<chapter xml:id="ch04-curves-coordinates-surfaces" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Curves, Coordinates, and Surfaces Before Calculus</title>

  <introduction>
    <p>This chapter uses algebra, trigonometry, and the vector geometry of Chapters 1<ndash/>3
    to describe curves and surfaces. We will evaluate parametrizations, choose domains,
    draw coordinate grids, and recognize repetitions before differentiating surfaces.</p>
  </introduction>

